(3. The main scan engine is a LangGraph workflow that branches by input type.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 590 Tm
(4. For repos, it first tries GitHub SBOM, then falls back to parsing dependency files) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 577 Tm
(   from the repo if needed.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 564 Tm
(5. Vulnerability matching is done mainly with OSV, and CVE details are enriched from) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 551 Tm
(   NVD.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 538 Tm
(6. In Detailed and Developer modes, the backend also enriches exact-version packages) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 525 Tm
(   with deps.dev metadata like licenses and useful links.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 512 Tm
(7. `/agent/chat` sits on top of the same backend and can use LLM stages for) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 499 Tm
(   interpretation and answer writing, but it can also fall back to deterministic) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 486 Tm
(   behavior if the LLM is unavailable.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 473 Tm
(8. The backend returns both a full JSON report and a compact `llm_context`, so the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 460 Tm
(   agent can respond cleanly without dumping raw provider payloads.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 435 Tm
(Demo script by input type) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 407 Tm
(#### Package query) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 382 Tm
(“When a user asks about a package, the controller or scan endpoint converts that into an) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 369 Tm
(exact package coordinate, runs vulnerability research, enriches metadata by mode, and) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 356 Tm
(then returns either a direct scan result or a conversational answer.”) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 331 Tm
(#### Repo URL) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 306 Tm
(“When a repo URL is sent, the system first tries GitHub SBOM. If that fails, it inspects) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 293 Tm
(the repo tree, fetches supported dependency files, parses them, and continues the scan) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 280 Tm
(from that normalized dependency list.”) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 255 Tm
(#### Dependency file upload) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 230 Tm
(“The backend expects the filename and file contents, not a raw binary upload. Once it) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 217 Tm
(receives those, it routes the content through the parser layer and then through the same) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 204 Tm
(vulnerability and enrichment pipeline.”) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 179 Tm
(#### LLM interaction) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
